WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.781
This is a fictional teaching example.

00:00:02.781 --> 00:00:10.197
A service team proposes an AI-assisted intake form that prepares a draft summary for human review.

00:00:10.197 --> 00:00:15.759
The purpose is clearer preparation, with faster processing still an unmeasured hypothesis.

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:26.420
Look at people: customers complete the intake, staff explain and check it, a reviewer approves the summary, and technical support handles form problems.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:33.372
Participation means inviting customers and staff to examine the proposed route while choices remain open.

00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:37.080
Support may include plain wording and staff-assisted intake.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:44.960
Responsibility stays with human roles: the service manager approves the route and the reviewer handles summary correction.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.058
Notice how each part of the lens changes the next question.

00:00:50.058 --> 00:00:54.230
Keep the draft-only boundary and record proposed benefits honestly.
